\caption(The union graph has five edges, with some projected segments overlapping on the line. Its shortest-path matrix is exactly the ordinary line-distance matrix; one Isomap axis recovers it.)
\alttext(Four labelled points lie on a horizontal line. A second panel shows their Isomap coordinate as a straight function of original position. Tables list the five edges, six pair distances and rank-one spectrum.)

>> A square cycle with a negative eigenvalue

Now take \((0,0),(1,0),(1,1),(0,1)\), again with \(k=2\). Every vertex selects
its two adjacent corners, so edges have length one and opposite corners have graph
distance two. Each squared-distance row has mean \(3/2\), giving

$$
 B=\tfrac14\begin{pmatrix}3&1&-5&1\\1&3&1&-5\\-5&1&3&1\\1&-5&1&3\end{pmatrix},
 \qquad \operatorname{eig}(B)=(2,2,0,-1).
$$
\alttext(The square-cycle geodesic Gram matrix has diagonal three quarters, adjacent entries one quarter and opposite entries minus five quarters. Its eigenvalues are two, two, zero and minus one.)

Two positive axes explain 100% of positive inertia. Yet the resulting square has adjacent
distances \(\sqrt2\), while opposite distances remain two. Its relative graph-distance
error is \((\sqrt2-1)/\sqrt3\), and its relative strain is \(1/3\). Negative
absolute-inertia mass is \(1/(2+2+1)=1/5\). Because the six pair distances have only
two distinct levels before and after embedding, their Pearson correlation is one.
Residual variance is therefore zero despite the edge distortion. All three diagnostics
must be read according to their definitions.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/isomap_square_cycle.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;d.add_column("x",std::vector<double>{0,1,1,0});d.add_column("y",std::vector<double>{0,0,1,1});
  const dm::stats::Isomap m(d,{"x","y"},{2,2});
  auto graph=m.neighborhood_graph().plot().title("Input cycle: unit edges").x_limits(-.936,1.936).y_limits(-.6,1.6);
  auto embedded=m.plot_embedding().title("Embedded edges: sqrt(2)").x_limits(-2.089,2.089).y_limits(-1.6,1.6);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(graph).add(embedded).size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/isomap_square_cycle.svg");
  std::print("{}\n\n{}\n",m.pair_distances().to_md(6),m.dimension_diagnostics().tail(1).to_md(6));
}
```
